{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new features and critical bug fixes to improve the robustness of string parsing. We are adding support for letter-only matching, slice access on results, and case-sensitive search options. Additionally, we have corrected issues with numeric type handling, brace enclosure validation, and timezone offset alignment.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The 'letters' format specifier must match only alphabetic characters, ensuring it does not match numeric digits like the 'w' specifier."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "Result instances must support the `__contains__` method, allowing users to check if a specific value or key exists within the result using the `in` operator."
    },
    {
      "id": "m05",
      "text": "The parser must validate that parts enclosed in braces are fully matched; unmatched or unenclosed braces should prevent successful parsing rather than silently matching."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "FixedTzOffset must correctly handle timezone offsets as defined in the associated bug fix, ensuring accurate parsing of time strings with fixed offsets."
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The parser must correctly interpret Fortran-formatted floating-point numbers, adhering to standard Fortran float syntax conventions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "text": "Hexadecimal, binary, and octal number formats must be parsed correctly, including proper detection of signed integers and automatic base detection where applicable."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23",
      "text": "The `findall` function must respect the `case_sensitive` argument, returning matches that strictly adhere to the specified case sensitivity setting."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25",
      "text": "Left-aligned and center-aligned searches must consume input up to the next whitespace character, ensuring correct boundary detection for formatted fields."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28",
      "text": "Result objects must support slice access, allowing users to retrieve subsets of matched values using standard Python slicing notation."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public APIs behave as described above to maintain consistency with the library's design goals. These changes address both usability enhancements and critical parsing errors."
}
